#' Municipal IPTU and ITBI Tax Revenue
#'
#' @description
#' Annual municipal IPTU and ITBI revenue in nominal BRL from SICONFI/FINBRA
#' DCA Annex I-C, 2013-present, with the 2018 account-vintage break marked by
#' account_scope; the Distrito Federal (5300108) is excluded because it
#' reports IPTU and ITBI only in its state-level accounts.
#'
#' Retrieve this dataset with [get_dataset()] using the name `"siconfi_taxes"`.
#'
#' ```r
#' siconfi_taxes <- get_dataset("siconfi_taxes")
#' ```
#'
#' @details
#' * **Source**: Tesouro Nacional - SICONFI (DCA, Anexo I-C) and FINBRA bulk files
#' * **URL**: <https://apidatalake.tesouro.gov.br/ords/siconfi/tt/entes>
#' * **Geography**: Brazilian municipalities
#' * **Frequency**: annual
#' * **Coverage**: 2013-latest closed year
#' * **Access mode**: `materialized`
#'
#' This dataset is cache-only: it is rebuilt by
#' data-raw/siconfi/build_snapshot.R from the maintainer's local FINBRA bulk
#' files (never in the repository) plus an API refresh of the latest years, so
#' source='fresh' and the fresh half of source='auto' do not apply. Values are
#' nominal BRL with a decimal-comma source parsed to the cent; the 2013 FINBRA
#' files include municipalities that filed QDCC instead of DCA (São Paulo
#' among them), accepted as published. The 2018 PCASP recode folds fines and
#' old-debt lines into the tax parents, so the pre-2018 tax line is not
#' comparable with the post-2018 tax family; account_scope marks the break and
#' no cross-break total is reconstructed. The Distrito Federal (5300108) is
#' excluded from the municipality universe because it reports IPTU and ITBI in
#' its state-level accounts and never in the municipal files. FUNDEB and
#' constitutional-transfer deduction columns never feed the tax deductions. A
#' municipality-year-tax with an observed gross row but no deduction row
#' counts the deduction as zero and computes net_revenue; deductions_reported
#' records whether a deduction row existed in the source. Municipalities
#' absent from a year's FINBRA file appear as non-reporters with
#' reported=FALSE and NA values.
#'
#' @section Columns:
#' \describe{
#'   \item{code_muni}{Seven-digit IBGE municipality code, geobr-compatible.}
#'   \item{abbrev_state}{Two-letter state abbreviation as published by the source.}
#'   \item{year}{Exercise year, 2013 to the latest closed year.}
#'   \item{tax}{Tax identifier: iptu or itbi.}
#'   \item{reported}{TRUE when the municipality appears in that year's data (FINBRA file or API refresh); non-reporters keep one NA row per tax.}
#'   \item{value_status}{observed (tax row present), missing_tax_row (the municipality reported but this tax has no gross row), or non_reporter (absent from the year's data).}
#'   \item{gross_revenue}{Realized gross tax-account value in nominal BRL; NA when the tax row is absent.}
#'   \item{other_deductions}{Non-FUNDEB, non-transfer tax deductions in nominal BRL; 0 when the municipality-year-tax has an observed gross row but no deduction row in the source, otherwise the observed value, kept even when the gross row is missing.}
#'   \item{deductions_reported}{TRUE when the source carried a deduction row for the municipality-year-tax; FALSE when only a gross row exists and the deduction is assumed 0; NA when the source has neither row.}
#'   \item{net_revenue}{Gross revenue minus deductions, rounded to cents, computed whenever the gross row exists (an assumed 0 deduction is subtracted).}
#'   \item{account_scope}{Account-vintage scope: legacy_line (IPTU and ITBI shown on separate account lines) through 2017, tax_family (post-2018 PCASP parents that fold in fines and old-debt lines) from 2018. Do not build a single constant-scope series across 2017-2018.}
#'   \item{source}{Row provenance: finbra (bulk-file history) or api (SICONFI API refresh of the latest years); NA for non-reporter rows.}
#' }
#'
#' @source Tesouro Nacional - SICONFI (DCA, Anexo I-C) and FINBRA bulk files
